# UK time format

Show **12-hour clock times** in British/Irish style for all visitor-facing salah, iqamah, programme, and schedule copy.

## Rules

| Rule | Example |
|------|---------|
| 12-hour clock | `4:30 pm`, not `16:30` |
| No leading zero on hour | `4:30 pm`, not `04:30 pm` |
| Lowercase `am` / `pm` | `7:00 am`, not `7:00 AM` |
| Minutes always two digits | `4:05 pm`, not `4:5 pm` |
| Space before period (HTML may use `&nbsp;` in tight UI) | `1:15 pm` |

## JavaScript

Use `formatUkDisplayTime()` in `scripts.js` — do not hand-roll or only call `.toLowerCase()` on API strings.

```javascript
formatUkDisplayTime("04:30 PM");           // 4:30 pm
formatUkDisplayTime("16:30");              // 4:30 pm (24h input)
formatUkDisplayTime("7:30", { nbspBeforePeriod: true }); // deck cards
```

Wrappers (all delegate to `formatUkDisplayTime`):

- `formatDeckTime` — home prayer deck (thin space before am/pm)
- `formatTimetableTime` — prayer-times page tables
- `formatTimeToAmPm` — Jumu'ah, Ramadan/Eid hero slots

Programme `clockTime` values must pass through `formatUkDisplayTime` in `getProgrammeTimeLabel` / `getProgrammeScheduleTime`.

## HTML

Static times in HTML: `4:00 pm`, `5:30 pm` — not `PM` or `04:00 PM`.

Nav/deck placeholders (`—`) are filled by JS; API times are normalised on display.

## Parsing

Internal parsing (`parseTimeOnRecord`, `parseTimeToDate`) accepts both 24-hour and 12-hour inputs — formatting is display-only.
